By eliminating tuition fees, lower-income students can pursue degrees in high-demand fields, leading to better-paying jobs and reducing the wealth gap.
Countries with free higher education, like Germany, show lower income inequality and higher social mobility, demonstrating the policy's effectiveness.
Free education allows individuals to invest in their future without financial barriers, creating a more skilled and diverse workforce.
When education is free, it reduces the intergenerational transmission of poverty, giving everyone a fairer start in life.
A more educated population leads to higher productivity and innovation, which can drive economic growth and reduce inequality.